WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:04.332
(fast paced guitar
strumming over cheering)

00:00:04.332 --> 00:00:05.488
- [Richard] From the very first time

00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:08.342
I did a run I was hooked.

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:11.894
It's a competition, and my
family, we're about competition.

00:00:11.894 --> 00:00:14.226
(fast paced guitar strumming)

00:00:14.226 --> 00:00:15.059
- When you get behind that horse,

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:17.097
and it doesn't matter how
many years you've done it,

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:18.765
you're a little bit worried, you know?

00:00:18.765 --> 00:00:20.061
Certain things can happen on that course

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:22.055
that could change your life forever.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:26.222
(fast paced guitar strumming with drums)

00:00:33.624 --> 00:00:35.277
(rider whoops)

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:38.701
(audience cheers and whistles)

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.463
Skijoring is basically
down on an 800 foot track

00:00:41.463 --> 00:00:43.970
with a horse that's towing you

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:47.196
going over three jumps,
getting three sets of rings,

00:00:47.196 --> 00:00:48.536
the fastest time wins.

00:00:48.536 --> 00:00:49.953
Boom, boom, boom.

00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:56.069
(fast paced guitar music)

00:00:56.069 --> 00:00:58.705
Sounds relatively easy,
but when you're doing

00:00:58.705 --> 00:01:01.985
40 miles an hour behind
this 1,500 pound animal,

00:01:01.985 --> 00:01:03.715
it gets to be really exciting.

00:01:03.715 --> 00:01:06.215
(banjo music)

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:11.587
- Skiers can crash, horses can crash

00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:14.019
and anything can happen.

00:01:14.019 --> 00:01:16.870
A lot can go wrong in 17 seconds.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.203
(fast guitar strumming)

00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:25.953
(slow guitar picking)

00:01:25.953 --> 00:01:27.400
I'm fourth generation on the ranch.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.763
(metal gate rattles)

00:01:29.763 --> 00:01:34.201
I was on a horse for my
first time at 24 hours old.

00:01:34.201 --> 00:01:36.458
I came back from the hospital
and my dad was on the horse,

00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:38.492
and so I got thrown up
on the horse with my dad,

00:01:38.492 --> 00:01:41.220
and since then I keep on riding.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.355
You guys ready to run?

00:01:42.355 --> 00:01:45.144
- I've been skiing since
I was two years old.

00:01:45.144 --> 00:01:46.842
(boot ratchets)

00:01:46.842 --> 00:01:50.245
Been racing, pi-gon skiing for 20 years.

00:01:50.245 --> 00:01:52.416
(skis thud)

00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:57.080
Skijoring is like no other
rush you've ever had.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.140
It is an adrenaline junky sport.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.345
(slow electronic music)

00:02:02.345 --> 00:02:03.675
- [Richard] You really
have to work together.

00:02:03.675 --> 00:02:05.154
It's teamwork, but you both gotta

00:02:05.154 --> 00:02:08.110
really know what you're doing to succeed.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.109
- We're ninth in the runaway.

00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:09.942
- Yep.

00:02:09.942 --> 00:02:11.405
- What we need to do is basically watch

00:02:11.405 --> 00:02:13.478
every runner before us.

00:02:13.478 --> 00:02:15.873
There are two different
cultures in this sport.

00:02:15.873 --> 00:02:19.689
- [Richard] You got a bunch of
rednecks or hicks or ranchers

00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:21.480
and you got a bunch of hippies.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.863
For this event, they get
together and they all get along.

00:02:23.863 --> 00:02:26.173
- Melding them together is important

00:02:26.173 --> 00:02:28.278
to become a full on team.

00:02:28.278 --> 00:02:29.138
- All out.

00:02:29.138 --> 00:02:30.321
- All out.

00:02:30.321 --> 00:02:31.478
Kick ass and take names.

00:02:31.478 --> 00:02:32.311
- Yep.

00:02:32.311 --> 00:02:34.150
(chuckles)

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:38.317
(low string music over electronic beat)

